    "answer": {
      "short": "Accept any one of these pairs: $\\frac{2}{7}$ and $\\frac{3}{8}$; $\\frac{3}{7}$ and $\\frac{2}{8}$; $\\frac{2}{7}$ and $\\frac{5}{8}$; $\\frac{5}{7}$ and $\\frac{2}{8}$. The clues do not identify a unique pair.",
      "worked": "The prime digits are chosen from $2,3,5,7$. The cube digit must be $8$: using $1$ would leave no common factor to cancel. Cancelling requires the prime digit $2$ together with $8$.\n\nThe following pairs satisfy every clue. Each fraction is proper, and cancelling $2$ with $8$ gives the simplified product.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{3}{8}&=\\frac{37}{56}<1\\\\\\frac{2}{7}\\times\\frac{3}{8}&=\\frac{1}{7}\\times\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3}{28}\\\\\\frac{3}{7}+\\frac{2}{8}&=\\frac{19}{28}<1\\\\\\frac{3}{7}\\times\\frac{2}{8}&=\\frac{3}{7}\\times\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{3}{28}\\\\\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{5}{8}&=\\frac{51}{56}<1\\\\\\frac{2}{7}\\times\\frac{5}{8}&=\\frac{1}{7}\\times\\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{5}{28}\\\\\\frac{5}{7}+\\frac{2}{8}&=\\frac{27}{28}<1\\\\\\frac{5}{7}\\times\\frac{2}{8}&=\\frac{5}{7}\\times\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{5}{28}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe digit sets are $2,3,7,8$ or $2,5,7,8$. Each has three prime digits and the cube digit $8$, and neither simplified product introduces a new digit. The clues allow more than one pair.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
